                <!-- JSON-2 Detail Section -->
                <section class="dics-kb-section">
                    <div class="dics-container">
                        <div class="dics-kb-engineering">
                            <div class="dics-kb-engineering__copy">
                                <span class="dics-kb-eyebrow">API MIGRATION CRITICAL PATH</span>
                                <h2>The JSON-2 Transaction Model — What Developers Must Know</h2>
                                <p>
                                    JSON-2 isn't just a syntax change. Each JSON-2 call runs in its own SQL
                                    transaction. Designing integrations as sequential API calls and assuming atomic
                                    behaviour will cause data inconsistency in Odoo 20. Odoo explicitly recommends
                                    using a single server-side business method for operations that must succeed or
                                    fail together.
                                </p>

                                <div class="dics-kb-pillars">
                                    <article>
                                        <span>01</span>
                                        <div>
                                            <h3>Bearer Auth &amp; Model Endpoints</h3>
                                            <p>Authenticate with an API key. Calls follow the pattern
                                                <code>POST /json/2/res.partner/search_read</code> — model and
                                                method in the URL, JSON body for parameters.</p>
                                        </div>
                                    </article>
                                    <article>
                                        <span>02</span>
                                        <div>
                                            <h3>One Transaction Per Call</h3>
                                            <p>Multi-step operations (reserve → update stock → create payment) must
                                                be wrapped in a single server-side method to guarantee
                                                transactional consistency.</p>
                                        </div>
                                    </article>
                                    <article>
                                        <span>03</span>
                                        <div>
                                            <h3>Audit Your Integration Stack</h3>
                                            <p>Identify all XML-RPC and JSON-RPC integrations. Test JSON-2
                                                equivalents, update authentication, validate permissions, and
                                                run transaction-level tests before migrating production.</p>
                                        </div>
                                    </article>
                                </div>
